From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Feiyang Yu <2541290956@qq.com>
Date: Sun, 15 Nov 2026 22:00:00 +0800
Subject: [PATCH] mtd: spinand: fmsh: add support for FM25LS01

FM25LS01 is a 1.8V 1Gbit SPI-NAND from Fudan Micro: 2048-byte pages
with 128 bytes of OOB, 64 pages per block, 1024 blocks, 1-bit on-die
ECC, no QE bit. Some H3C NX30-family and HW3000B1 routers ship with it.

The geometry, ECC requirement and OOB layout (user bytes 2-63, ECC in
64-127, same as FM25G01B) follow the FM25LS01 entry of the Rockchip
vendor kernel. Read the ECC status with the generic helper, as the
vendor driver does.

Signed-off-by: Feiyang Yu <2541290956@qq.com>
---
--- a/drivers/mtd/nand/spi/fmsh.c
+++ b/drivers/mtd/nand/spi/fmsh.c
@@ -235,6 +235,15 @@ static const struct spinand_info fmsh_sp
 		     SPINAND_HAS_QE_BIT,
 		     SPINAND_ECCINFO(&fm25s01bi3_ooblayout,
 				      fm25s01bi3_ecc_get_status)),
+	SPINAND_INFO("FM25LS01",
+		     SPINAND_ID(SPINAND_READID_METHOD_OPCODE_DUMMY, 0xa5),
+		     NAND_MEMORG(1, 2048, 128, 64, 1024, 20, 1, 1, 1),
+		     NAND_ECCREQ(1, 512),
+		     SPINAND_INFO_OP_VARIANTS(&read_cache_variants,
+					      &write_cache_variants,
+					      &update_cache_variants),
+		     0,
+		     SPINAND_ECCINFO(&fm25g01b_ooblayout, NULL)),
 };
 
 static const struct spinand_manufacturer_ops fmsh_spinand_manuf_ops = {
